module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.UnboundedGlobalSections
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# The second spectral sequence of Tag 0BLX for a nilpotent ideal sheaf

Let `A` be a ring, `I ⊂ A` a finitely generated ideal, `(𝒞, 𝒪)` a ringed site with `𝒪` a sheaf
of `A`-algebras, `𝓘 = I𝒪` the ideal sheaf `I` generates and `ℱ` a sheaf of `𝒪`-modules. This
file proves the second spectral sequence of [Stacks, Tag 0BLX],
`E₂^{p,q} = H^p(𝒞, H^q(ℱ^∧))` abutting to `H^{p+q}(RΓ(𝒞, ℱ^∧))`, in the regime of
`UnboundedGlobalSections.lean`: the local sections of `I𝒪` nilpotent. There `ℱ^∧` is bounded
below, being `ℱ` itself in degree zero, so the spectral sequence of [Stacks, Tag 015J] applies to
it.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite`
  `.exists_pages_derivedCompletion_globalSections_of_forall_isNilpotent`:
  **the second spectral sequence of [Stacks, Tag 0BLX]** in that regime, with both inputs that
  `GlobalSectionsCompletion.lean` has to assume — [Stacks, Tag 099F] and a bounded below
  representative of `ℱ^∧` — produced from the nilpotence hypothesis.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BLX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BLX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 015I](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/015I)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 015J](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/015J)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

variable (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A) (X : RingedSite.{u, u, u})
  (ρ : A →+* RingCat.sectionsSubring ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj)
  (𝓘 : SheafOfModules.Submodule
    (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))))

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0BLX], the second spectral sequence**, for an ideal sheaf whose local sections
are nilpotent. Let `A` be a ring, `I ⊂ A` a finitely generated ideal, `(𝒞, 𝒪)` a ringed site with
`𝒪` a sheaf of `A`-algebras, `𝓘 = I𝒪` the ideal sheaf `I` generates and `ℱ` a sheaf of
`𝒪`-modules. Write `ℱ^∧` for the derived completion of `ℱ` along `I𝒪`. Then `ℱ` in degree zero
*is* a bounded below representative of `ℱ^∧`, and for a Cartan-Eilenberg resolution of it the
second spectral sequence of [Stacks, Tag 015J] for `Γ(𝒞, -)` has
```
E₂^{p,q} = H^p(𝒞, H^q(ℱ^∧))
```
and abuts to `H^{p+q}(RΓ(𝒞, ℱ^∧))`, which is `H^{p+q}(𝒞, ℱ^∧)`.

Both of the inputs that
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_pages_derivedCompletion_globalSections` of
`GlobalSectionsCompletion.lean` *assumes* are here produced from the nilpotence hypothesis, which
is a restriction on the data and not a part of the source's conclusion:

* [Stacks, Tag 099F], the existence of `(-)^∧` on `D(𝒪)`, is
  `isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_of_forall_isNilpotent` of `NilpotentIdeal.lean`; the
  instance is produced inside the statement, exactly as in
  `exists_iso_derivedCompletion_derivedGlobalSections` above.
* The bounded below representative of `ℱ^∧` is `ℱ` itself in degree zero: every object of `D(𝒪)`
  is derived complete along such an ideal sheaf, so `K ⟶ K^∧` is invertible at `ℱ[0]`, and a
  complex concentrated in degree zero is bounded below, being strictly `≥ 0`. That isomorphism
  is the first conclusion below, so
  the statement itself says that `ℱ^∧` is bounded below here rather than assuming it.

Both inputs are also produced at an `I𝒪` generated by finitely many global sections of `𝒪`:
that is `exists_pages_derivedCompletion_globalSections_generatedIdealSheaf` of
`GlobalSectionsCompletionGenerated.lean`, the reflector being the Čech completion of
[Stacks, Tag 099B] and `Č(f)` being bounded. This theorem is the nilpotent instance of
`exists_pages_derivedCompletion_globalSections`.
The Cartan-Eilenberg resolution is a hypothesis for the reason Tag 015J takes one, its existence
being [Stacks, Tag 015I]. -/
@[stacks 0BLX "the second spectral sequence, `E₂^{p,q} = H^p(𝒞, H^q(ℱ^∧))` abutting to
  `H^{p+q}(RΓ(𝒞,ℱ^∧))`, for an ideal sheaf `I𝒪` whose local sections are nilpotent — the regime in
  which `ℱ[0]` is a bounded below representative of `ℱ^∧`; that representative and
  [Stacks, Tag 099F] are both produced from that hypothesis rather than assumed. At the source's
  own generality the same statement is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_pages_derivedCompletion_globalSections_generatedIdealSheaf`,
  every `I𝒪` of a finitely generated `I` being generated by finitely many global sections of `𝒪`"]
theorem exists_pages_derivedCompletion_globalSections_of_forall_isNilpotent
    (hI : I.FG) (h𝓘 : IsIdealSheafGeneratedBy A I X ρ 𝓘)
    (hnil : ∀ (V : X.C) (g : ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj.obj (op V)),
      g ∈ 𝓘.toSubmodule.obj (op V) → IsNilpotent g)
    (F : SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))
    (Ires : ((CochainComplex.singleFunctor
      (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) 0).obj
      F).CartanEilenbergResolution) :
    letI : (ObjectProperty.ι (IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} X 𝓘)).IsRightAdjoint :=
      isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_of_forall_isNilpotent X 𝓘 hnil
    let L := (((moduleGlobalSectionsOver X A ρ).mapHomologicalComplex
      (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).mapHomologicalComplex (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).obj Ires.bicomplex
    Nonempty (DerivedCategory.Q.obj
        ((CochainComplex.singleFunctor
          (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) 0).obj F) ≅
      (derivedCompletion X 𝓘).obj
        ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor
          (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) 0).obj F)) ∧
    (∀ p q : ℤ, Nonempty ((L.homology q).homology p ≅
      (siteCohomologyOver X A ρ p).obj
        ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor
          (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) q).obj
          ((derivedCompletion X 𝓘).obj
            ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor
              (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) 0).obj F))))) ∧
    ∀ n : ℤ, Nonempty ((HomologicalComplex₂.total L (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).homology n ≅
      (DerivedCategory.Plus.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} A) n).obj
        ((derivedGlobalSectionsOver X A ρ).obj (DerivedCategory.Plus.Q.obj
          ⟨(CochainComplex.singleFunctor
            (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) 0).obj F,
            ⟨0, inferInstance⟩⟩))) := by
  let : (ObjectProperty.ι (IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} X 𝓘)).IsRightAdjoint :=
    isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_of_forall_isNilpotent X 𝓘 hnil
  have hiso : IsIso ((derivedCompletionUnit X 𝓘).app
      ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor
        (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) 0).obj F)) :=
    isIso_derivedCompletionUnit_app X 𝓘
      (isDerivedComplete_of_forall_isNilpotent X 𝓘 hnil _)
  have eK : DerivedCategory.Q.obj
        ((CochainComplex.singleFunctor
          (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) 0).obj F) ≅
      (derivedCompletion X 𝓘).obj
        ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor
          (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) 0).obj F) :=
    ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctorIsoCompQ
        (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) 0).app F).symm ≪≫
      asIso ((derivedCompletionUnit X 𝓘).app
        ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor
          (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) 0).obj F))
  obtain ⟨hE₂, hTot⟩ := exists_pages_derivedCompletion_globalSections A I X ρ 𝓘 hI h𝓘 F
    ((CochainComplex.singleFunctor
      (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) 0).obj F)
    ⟨0, inferInstance⟩ eK Ires
  exact ⟨⟨eK⟩, hE₂, hTot⟩


end AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

end
